## 1. PIECE 1 — ADMIN & CATALOG (use Refine, don't hand-build)

**Decision:** do NOT build an admin panel screen-by-screen in the app. Point
**Refine** (open-source React admin framework, free for self-hosting) at your
existing Supabase database and it generates working CRUD pages in minutes. This
is a SEPARATE small web app from the mobile app — admins use a browser, not the
phone.

Cursor: scaffold a Refine + Supabase admin project in a `/admin` folder (or a
separate repo), using the current `@refinedev/supabase` data provider pointed at
the same Supabase project. Generate resources for these existing tables:

- **clinics** — need a new table (Section 2 SQL below)
- **doctors** — new table (Section 2)
- **products** (from Phase 3) — tests + supplements catalog
- **orders / order_items** (from Phase 3) — view + update fulfilment status
- **test_orders / test_results** (Phase 1/2) — view, and upload/confirm results
- **interventions** (Phase 2) — the review queue (Piece 2)
- **profiles** — patient list, read-mostly
- **clinical thresholds** — surface `lib/clinical-thresholds.ts` values as an editable table (Section 2) so a clinician can change TSH/BMI/insulin cut-offs without code

For the non-coder: once Refine is generated, adding a clinic or changing a test
price is a form in a browser — no SQL, no code. This replaces the "manage from
Supabase Table Editor" interim from earlier phases.

