## 7. PHASE 4 ERROR-PROOFING ADDITIONS

- [ ] Role-based RLS verified: a clinician cannot query patients they aren't linked to; clinic_staff cannot see clinical results.
- [ ] Plan sign-off is authorised server-side (clinician + `can_sign_off`), never from the client.
- [ ] Rules engine reads thresholds from DB but falls back to the code file on fetch failure — never crashes, never blank.
- [ ] Lab integration sits behind the `LabProvider` interface; `ManualLabProvider` keeps the app working with no live lab.
- [ ] Lab and Stripe and Expo-push secrets live ONLY in Edge Function secrets, never in app or admin client code.
- [ ] Notifications degrade gracefully when permission is denied — app fully usable without them.
- [ ] The recurring symptom check still routes any "yes" to Pathway B.
- [ ] Push requires an EAS dev/prod build — the founder has been told Expo Go won't work for this, and this is also the pre-store-submission build.
- [ ] SQL went in the SQL editor; all provider/push/sign-off TypeScript went in Edge Functions.

